{{!--
    OVERRIDE of swagger-codegen's stock typescript-angular/modelGeneric.mustache.
    The ONLY change is the inverted additionalPropertiesType section wrapped
    around the "extends parent" clause below; everything else is the stock
    template and should be kept in sync with it on a codegen upgrade.

    Why: for a schema that is a pure map - "type: object" plus
    additionalProperties, with NO properties of its own - DefaultCodegenConfig
    marks the model isMapModel and sets parent = toInstantiationType(schema),
    which builds instantiationTypes.get("map") + "<String, " + innerType + ">".
    The TypeScript generators never register a "map" instantiation type, so that
    lookup returns null and the parent becomes the literal string
    "null<String, any>". The stock template emits it verbatim and the library
    then fails to compile:

        export interface PipelineEnvironment extends null<String, any> {
        error TS2499: An interface can only extend an identifier/qualified-name
                      with optional type arguments.

    brain's PipelineEnvironment (ai.gebo.llms.chat.client.rest.model.PipelineRequestBody)
    is exactly that shape: a Schema annotation with additionalProperties TRUE
    over a hidden JsonAnyGetter map, so springdoc emits
    {"type":"object","additionalProperties":true} with no properties. The java
    generator renders it correctly as "extends HashMap<String, Object>"; only
    typescript-angular breaks, which is why this override lives here and not in
    the java-resttemplate templates.

    Suppressing the parent loses nothing: a map model's entries are already
    emitted by the modelGenericAdditionalProperties partial as an index
    signature - "[key: string]: any" - which is how TypeScript spells that
    inheritance. The guard is deliberately narrow, keyed on
    additionalPropertiesType rather than dropping "extends" outright, so a
    genuine allOf/composed parent - which has no additionalPropertiesType -
    still renders.
--}}
export interface {{classname}} {{^additionalPropertiesType}}{{#parent}}extends {{{parent}}} {{/parent}}{{/additionalPropertiesType}}{ {{>modelGenericAdditionalProperties}}
{{#vars}}
    {{#description}}
    /**
     * {{{description}}}
     */
    {{/description}}
    {{#is this 'read-only'}}readonly {{/is}}{{name}}{{^required}}?{{/required}}: {{#is this 'enum'}}{{{datatypeWithEnum}}}{{/is}}{{#isNot this 'enum'}}{{{datatype}}}{{/isNot}};
{{/vars}}
}{{>modelGenericEnums}}